        <mxCell id="header-sub" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#1e293b&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;What may reach a project&amp;#39;s workloads and the tunnel relays on each cluster, and what enforces it?&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;Scope: ingress to one project&amp;#39;s namespaces on on-prem (K3s), EKS and GKE, the cloud perimeter and the cloud end of the tunnel relays · main as of 2026-10-29 · derived from code; project matrix of 18/10 checked live (marked live)&lt;br&gt;Out of scope: egress (open everywhere) · the hub&amp;#39;s own namespaces, except the on-prem end of the relays (card) · admission of tenant workloads beyond the cloud guardrails. Drawn as a topology: a matrix holds grants, not network rules.&lt;br&gt;v0.2 · source: cnp-docs/architecture/cnp&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
